Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:40:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 140/143] config: enable USB printer support (usblp) and the
 parallel port stack
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A user with a legacy USB laser printer (an HP LaserJet GDI model)
reported that the kernel has no way to talk to it (github issue #5):
USB_PRINTER was never enabled, so /dev/usb/lp0 is not created and CUPS
and the foo2zjs firmware downloader have nothing to open.

Enable USB_PRINTER=m, the USB printer class driver, which covers USB
printers and USB-to-Centronics printer cables.

The reporter also asked for PPDEV "for parallel port emulation over USB
just in case", without saying which adapter. Cover that path too: enable
the parport subsystem (PARPORT=m, with IEEE-1284 status readback) plus
the three drivers that sit on it — lp (PRINTER=m, /dev/lp0 for classic
Centronics printers), ppdev (PPDEV=m, userspace /dev/parportN access)
and parport_uss720 (USB_USS720=m, the USS720-style USB-to-parallel
adapters that expose a raw parallel port instead of a printer-class
device). The board has no native parallel port, so all of this only
comes alive through a USB adapter.

Everything is a module, so the Image is unchanged and nothing loads
unless matching hardware is plugged in.

Verified with a defconfig -> .config roundtrip: only the six symbols
above change.

Link: https://github.com/ut-slayer/orangepi-4a-mainline/issues/5
Reported-by: ascold113 <https://github.com/ascold113>
Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
index 69b930790..c8583dc62 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
@@ -226,6 +226,8 @@ CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR=y
 CONFIG_MTD_UBI=m
 CONFIG_MTD_HYPERBUS=m
 CONFIG_OF_OVERLAY=y
+CONFIG_PARPORT=m
+CONFIG_PARPORT_1284=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM=m
 CONFIG_ZRAM_BACKEND_LZ4=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM_BACKEND_LZ4HC=y
@@ -406,6 +408,8 @@ CONFIG_SERIAL_FSL_LPUART_CONSOLE=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_FSL_LINFLEXUART=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_FSL_LINFLEXUART_CONSOLE=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_BUS=y
+CONFIG_PRINTER=m
+CONFIG_PPDEV=m
 CONFIG_IPMI_HANDLER=m
 CONFIG_IPMI_DEVICE_INTERFACE=m
 CONFIG_IPMI_SI=m
@@ -759,6 +763,7 @@ CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD_PLATFORM=y
 CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD_PLATFORM=y
 CONFIG_USB_ACM=m
+CONFIG_USB_PRINTER=m
 CONFIG_USB_STORAGE=y
 CONFIG_USB_CDNS_SUPPORT=m
 CONFIG_USB_CDNS3=m
@@ -776,6 +781,7 @@ CONFIG_USB_SERIAL=m
 CONFIG_USB_SERIAL_CP210X=m
 CONFIG_USB_SERIAL_FTDI_SIO=m
 CONFIG_USB_SERIAL_OPTION=m
+CONFIG_USB_USS720=m
 CONFIG_USB_HSIC_USB3503=y
 CONFIG_USB_ONBOARD_DEV=m
 CONFIG_NOP_USB_XCEIV=y
